  "$comment": "Committed warm-load allowlist for invoke.from_argv's params.entrypoint (coordinator_core/ops/invoke_from_argv.py). A name absent from this list refuses (fail closed) rather than warm-loading an unvetted CLI's module body into the shared server process ~50 concurrent sessions share. REGENERATED (chunk C2 fix) each run from forwarder_door_census.py's 'door-eligible' bucket over the full generator-known coordinator/bin/ population, unioned only with the fixed _C1_SEEDED_NAMES tuple (C1's seeded proving CLI) -- never unioned with this file's own prior content, which is how a 12-name origin count silently reached 382. See docs/research/spike-verdicts/2026-08-27-multi-name-native-invocation-surface.md, chunks C0-C2. C5 DISPOSITION (2026-08-27): 12 rows named coordinator/bin CLIs that exist only as extensionless files (chunk-commits, claim-neighbours, coordinator-ensure-hooks-fleet, coordinator-postsync-marker-resync-check, coordinator-precommit-foreign-platform-check, coordinator-precommit-settings-tracking-check, gate-validate-invocable, plan-tasks-resolve, plan-tasks-stamp, spawn-census, static-check, with-suite-mutex) -- _resolve_entrypoint_script and serve_classifier both hardcode coordinator/bin/<name>.py, so none of these twelve ever resolved (confirmed no_script in the C8 ratchet baseline, test_every_allowlisted_name_warm_serves.py). Retired here rather than left recorded: an allowlist row naming a path with nothing on it today is reviewless warm-service the instant a .py file lands at that path later. forwarder_door_census.py own door-eligible bucket does not yet model the .py-suffix requirement for extensionless CLIs, so a regen before that is fixed will re-emit these twelve -- see docs/research/spike-verdicts/2026-08-27-multi-name-native-invocation-surface.md. HAND-ADDED ROW (2026-08-28): 'handoff-housekeeping' was added by hand rather than by a --write-allowlist regen. It classifies door-eligible on its own evidence (classify_one -> op_equivalent=True, warm_loadable=True, no evidence rows) and is generator-known (_derive_agent_helper_target_map resolves it to handoff-housekeeping.py), so a regen WOULD emit it -- but the same regen also re-emits the twelve extensionless names the C5 DISPOSITION above retired, because forwarder_door_census still does not model the .py-suffix requirement. Measured 2026-08-28: a regen adds exactly those twelve plus this name and drops nothing. One hand-added row is the smaller defect than silently reinstating twelve retired ones; fix the census's suffix modelling and this note retires with the hand-edit. Warm-serve is proven for this name by coordinator_core/warm/tests/test_handoff_housekeeping_warm_serves.py, not by this row.",
